<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Buchanan (governor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1808–1841</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas Buchanan was an American colonisation agent who became governor of Bassa Cove in 1836 and in 1839 the first governor of the Commonwealth of Liberia, which united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monrovia">Monrovia</a>, Bassa Cove and other settlements. A cousin of the future US president James Buchanan, he organised the militia and fought local rulers who traded in slaves. He died of fever in 1841 and was succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-jenkins-roberts">Joseph Jenkins Roberts</a>.</p></div>
